build(ch, "light-heat-sound", "Light, heat and sound", 35,
    ["Explain why shadows form and tell transparent, translucent and opaque materials apart.", "Describe how heat moves and name good conductors and insulators of heat.", "Explain that sound is made by vibrations and travels through materials."],
    [("key", "definition", "Light", "We see things when light from a **source** (the sun, a lamp, a fire) or **reflected** by an object (like the moon) enters our eyes. **Light travels in straight lines.** **Transparent** materials let light through (clear glass, clean water). **Translucent** ones let some light through (frosted glass, tissue paper). **Opaque** ones block light (wood, metal). A **shadow** forms when an opaque object blocks light."),
     ("fig", fig_light, "A shadow forms behind an opaque object.", "A lamp on the left sends three rays to the right. A grey object blocks the rays. Behind it there is a grey shadow."),
     ("key", "definition", "Heat", "**Heat** moves from a **hotter** place to a **colder** one. In **solids** (metals) it moves by conduction: a metal spoon in hot tea becomes hot. In **liquids and air** hot parts rise (convection). The **sun's heat** reaches us across space (radiation). **Conductors** (metals) let heat pass easily; **insulators** (wood, plastic, cloth) do not. Temperature is measured with a thermometer in **degrees Celsius (°C)**."),
     ("key", "definition", "Sound", "**Sound** is made when things **vibrate** (move quickly to and fro): a drum skin, a guitar string, our vocal cords. Sound travels through air, water and solids, but **not through empty space**. A **high pitch** comes from fast vibrations, a **loud** sound from big vibrations. An **echo** is sound that bounces off a hard surface. Light travels much faster than sound, so we see lightning before we hear thunder."),
     ("key", "pieges", "Common mistakes", "- Saying that a metal pot handle is made of metal because it is a good **insulator**: metal is a conductor, so handles are made of wood or plastic.\n- Saying that the moon is a source of light: it **reflects** the sun's light.\n- Saying that sound needs no material to travel through.\n- Looking at the sun directly or with sunglasses only: it can damage the eyes."),
     ("ex", "Example 1", "Why do cooking pots have handles of wood or plastic?", ["The metal of the pot is a good conductor, so the heat travels to the handle.", "Wood and plastic are insulators, so the handle stays cool and we can hold it."], "Because wood and plastic are insulators: they do not let the heat pass, so the handle stays cool."),
     ("ex", "Example 2", "You see lightning and hear thunder a few seconds later. Why?", ["Light travels much faster than sound.", "The light reaches us almost at once; the sound takes longer."], "Light travels faster than sound.")],
    [M("application", "Which material is opaque?", "wood", ["clear glass", "clean water", "clear plastic"], "Opaque materials block light."),
     M("application", "Sound is made when something...", "vibrates", ["is cold", "is still", "is transparent"], "Vibrations make sound."),
     M("application", "Which is a good conductor of heat?", "a metal spoon", ["a wooden spoon", "a plastic cup", "a cloth"], "Metals conduct heat well."),
     TF("approfondissement", "Sound can travel through water.", True, "Sound travels through solids, liquids and gases."),
     MA("approfondissement", "Match the word with its meaning.", [("transparent", "lets light pass through"), ("opaque", "blocks light"), ("conductor", "lets heat pass easily"), ("echo", "sound that bounces back")], "These are the key words."),
     P("Mary holds a metal spoon in a pot of hot soup. After a minute the end she is holding is hot. She changes to a wooden spoon and her hand stays cool.",
       [PM("Why did the metal spoon become hot?", "metal is a good conductor of heat", ["metal is an insulator", "metal is transparent", "the spoon was shiny"], "Heat moves along metal."),
        PM("Why did the wooden spoon stay cool?", "wood is a poor conductor (an insulator)", ["wood is opaque", "wood makes sound", "wood is a liquid"], "Wood does not let heat pass easily."),
        PM("How does heat move along the spoon?", "from the hot end to the cold end", ["from the cold end to the hot end", "it does not move", "only upwards in air"], "Heat flows from hot to cold.", points=2)])],
    [("A shadow is formed when light is blocked by an...", "opaque object", ["transparent object", "clear glass", "mirror only"], "Opaque things block light."),
     ("Which travels fastest?", "light", ["sound", "a bicycle", "wind"], "Light is much faster than sound."),
     ("Heat moves from...", "hot to cold", ["cold to hot", "nowhere", "up only"], "From the hotter place to the colder place."),
     ("Which material is an insulator of heat?", "plastic", ["copper", "iron", "aluminium"], "Plastic is a poor conductor."),
     ("Sound cannot travel through...", "empty space", ["water", "air", "wood"], "It needs a material.")],
    ["Standard textbook facts only; temperature of boiling/freezing and speeds of light and sound are deliberately left out."],
    prereq=["fslc-science-matter-energy"])

